WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.700
Better money habits: change a habit, borrow wisely, and spot scams.

2
00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:09.250
This is the video for Module 4, Building Better Financial Habits.

3
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:19.190
Most money problems come from small habits repeated many times: a daily snack, a weekly bet, lending without writing anything down.

4
00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:24.340
A habit is a loop. The cue is the trigger, like payday or a WhatsApp status.

5
00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:28.640
The routine is what you do, such as buying something.

6
00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:32.470
The reward is the good feeling afterwards.

7
00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:38.920
To change a habit, keep the cue and the reward, but swap the routine for a better one.

8
00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:48.370
For example, Chinwe, a civil servant in Owerri, went to the mall with friends every payday and spent about 35,000 naira.

9
00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:58.640
Now, on payday morning, she moves 25,000 naira to savings first, then meets her friends for a cheaper outing with a set 8,000 naira.

10
00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:09.610
Over 12 months she saves about 300,000 naira, and still enjoys time with friends. She kept the cue and the reward. That is why the change lasted.

11
00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:17.950
Before borrowing, ask for three numbers in writing: how much you receive, how much you repay in total, and by when.

12
00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:37.110
For example, Ruth needs about 50,000 naira for stock. A digital lender wants 62,500 back in 30 days. That costs 12,500, which is 25 percent for one month. The stock will earn her only about 10,000, so she would lose money.

13
00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:50.690
Her registered cooperative wants 5,500 a month for 10 months, 55,000 in total. The cost is 5,000 naira, and she still gains. Ruth chooses Loan B.

14
00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:56.290
Compare the total amount repaid, not just the monthly payment or the speed of approval.

15
00:01:57.540 --> 00:02:07.550
Know these three scams. First, someone promises a loan or grant but asks for a processing, insurance or registration fee first. Do not pay.

16
00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:16.990
Second, callers claim to be from your bank and ask for your BVN, card details, PIN or OTP. Banks never ask for these.

17
00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:32.060
Third, ponzi schemes. They pay earlier members with money from newer members, not real profits. MMM Nigeria froze members' accounts in December 2016, and many lost their savings.

18
00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:43.720
Warning signs are guaranteed high returns, pressure to act fast, rewards for recruiting, payment into a personal account, and no registration with SEC Nigeria.

19
00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:57.150
Check loan apps on the FCCPC list, investment platforms with SEC Nigeria, and banks with the CBN. An app that wants all your contacts and photos is a warning sign.

20
00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:11.350
If you have sent money to a fraudster, contact your bank immediately through its official channels and report to the police. And if betting is taking over in your home, delete the apps, tell a trusted person, and seek support.

21
00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:19.980
Goals give your saving a direction. A SMART goal is specific, measurable, achievable, relevant and time-bound.

22
00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:31.720
For example, Hauwa makes kunu and zobo in Zaria. She will save about 180,000 naira for a second cooking pot, a chest cooler and packaging by 30 June.

23
00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:40.140
180,000 divided by 9 months is about 20,000 a month, or about 5,000 a week.

24
00:03:41.390 --> 00:03:53.910
Every Friday she saves 5,000 into a locked plan before restocking, and records the balance on a wall chart. Build your emergency fund first, then move on to exciting goals like this.

25
00:03:55.160 --> 00:04:05.460
Children learn money habits mostly by watching adults. For example, Ifeoma gives her son Chidi about 1,000 naira a week for sweeping and washing plates.

26
00:04:06.710 --> 00:04:13.160
They agree on three jars: 500 naira to Save, 300 to Spend, and 200 to Share.

27
00:04:14.410 --> 00:04:22.940
Chidi wants a football costing about 5,000 naira. With 500 a week, he gets there in 10 weeks, and buys it with his own money.

28
00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:30.100
Teach older children never to share PINs or OTPs, and never to click links promising free money.

29
00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:40.520
Now change one money habit, do your debt and scam check, write your goal plan, and start a money habit with a child. Continue with the lessons below.
